  <prompt>
    Deploy the NDA advisory vertical: BFF (bff-deploy), SpaarkeAi code page (code-page-deploy), Dataverse
    Actions/Bindings (dataverse-deploy), and the AI Search index seed. Enforce the ≤60 MB BFF publish-size gate
    before deploying the API.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE release engineer. Expert in the bff-deploy / code-page-deploy / dataverse-deploy skills and the
    add-reference-to-index flow. Follow azure-deployment.md.
  </role>

  <goal>
    All surfaces are deployed and reachable in the target environment; the end-to-end flow works against deployed
    infrastructure; BFF publish size is ≤60 MB and recorded.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Deliverables: BFF endpoints/services, SpaarkeAi client, Dataverse Actions + Binding rows, AI Search index
      content. Deploy in dependency order (index + Dataverse before client verification).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/</file>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>All implementation + eval tasks.</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="azure-deployment.md">Run `dotnet publish -c Release` and confirm compressed output ≤60 MB before deploying the BFF; record absolute size + diff vs baseline. HARD STOP at 60 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-9">No secrets in config; use Key Vault for production secrets.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Deploy Dataverse Actions/Bindings + the AI Search seed before verifying the client flow. Follow each deploy skill's own prescriptive steps.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/ENVIRONMENT-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Run the BFF publish-size check; HARD STOP if &gt;60 MB. Record size + diff.</step>
    <step order="2">Deploy the AI Search index seed (NDA standard) if not already in the target env.</step>
    <step order="3">Deploy Dataverse Actions + Binding rows (dataverse-deploy / seed scripts).</step>
    <step order="4">Deploy the BFF (bff-deploy).</step>
    <step order="5">Deploy the SpaarkeAi code page (code-page-deploy).</step>
    <step order="6">Smoke-test end-to-end against the deployed environment.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 060 ✅; record deployment + size in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If BFF publish size exceeds 60 MB, STOP (HARD STOP per azure-deployment.md) and escalate for architecture review before deploying.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Publish the BFF.</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run deploy skills/scripts.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build the code page.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-nda-r1/notes/ (deployment record + publish size)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish compressed size is ≤60 MB and recorded; deploy proceeds only if under the ceiling.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF, code page, Dataverse Actions/Bindings, and AI Search index are deployed and reachable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A deployed-environment smoke test of the end-to-end NDA flow succeeds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No secrets are committed; production secrets are in Key Vault.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Prescriptive/ordered — deploy dependencies before dependents. Coordinate with any external Reasoning-deployment
